title: "Renascor: An open catalogue of digital editions of Renaissance-era written documents"
message: "If you use this catalogue in your research, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23345610
authors:
  - family-names: Godbarge
    given-names: Clément
    affiliation: "University of St Andrews"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8699-7582"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23345610
    description: "Concept DOI for all versions, archived on Zenodo"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pantagrueliste/renascor"
url: "https://pantagrueliste.github.io/renascor/"
abstract: >-
  Renascor is an open catalogue of freely accessible digital editions and text
  collections of written documents from 1450 to 1700 (manuscripts, printed
  works, correspondence, inscriptions). Each record describes the project behind
  a collection: scope, period, languages, countries, text format, licence,
  editors, access links and DOI where available, with text and word counts
  derived from the Renascor Corpus. The catalogue can be browsed online and
  downloaded as CSV, JSON or BibTeX.
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - renaissance
  - digital editions
